  "question": {
    "text": "A plane EM wave is propagating along $x$ direction. It has a wavelength of $4 \\mathrm{~mm}$. If electric field is in $y$ direction with the maximum magnitude of $60 \\mathrm{Vm}^{-1}$, the equation for magnetic field is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4nNsC",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{B}_z=2 \\times 10^{-7} \\sin \\left[\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\times 10^3\\left(x-3 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{t}\\right)\\right] \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9c52I",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{B}_z=60 \\sin \\left[\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\left(x-3 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{t}\\right)\\right] \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CJhZS",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{B}_x=60 \\sin \\left[\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\left(x-3 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{t}\\right)\\right] \\hat{\\mathrm{i} ~ T}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "afS28",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{B}_z=2 \\times 10^{-7} \\sin \\left[\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\left(x-3 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{t}\\right)\\right] \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{E}=\\mathrm{BC} \\Rightarrow 60=\\mathrm{B} \\times 3 \\times 10^8$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{B}=2 \\times 10^{-7}$\nAlso $\\quad \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{f} \\lambda$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow 3 \\times 10^8=\\mathrm{f} \\times 4 \\times 10^{-3} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}=\\frac{3}{4} \\times 10^{11} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\omega=2 \\pi \\mathrm{f}=\\frac{3}{4} \\times 2 \\pi \\times 10^{11} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\omega=\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{C}\\end{aligned}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad$ Electric field $\\Rightarrow y$ direction\nPropagation $\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}$ direction\nMagnetic field $\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{z}$-direction",
    "image": null
  },
